  "The sea lions on Pier 39's K-dock (src/client/sealions.ts): draw-only, never in the sim. The city export lists them",
  "(city.sealions: [{ x, y, z, heading, length, roll, pile, layer }], site metres, z the deck under the belly, heading in compass degrees like",
  "the spots: 0 north (+y), 90 east; length in metres, roll in degrees (over 15: lying on its side), pile: the group on one float,",
  "layer: 0 on the float, 1 and up on another's back); 'test' holds the phase-11 positions for the unit tests. size: body length in metres when the export gives none (seeded). poses: shares of flat, head up and rolled",
  "on its side. drawDistance: metres from the camera to the dock beyond which nothing is drawn or updated (times the",
  "preset's drawDistance); animate: metres within which they move; low: share drawn on low (presets.sealions).",
  "barkFar: barks only with the player this near; barkEvery: seconds between barks; shuffleEvery, flopEvery: seconds",
  "between a sea lion's shuffle and its flop into the water (per sea lion, seeded); under: seconds under water; dive:",
  "metres past the pile's edge and below the deck."
